# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# A tab button goes DOWN under the hand and does its work when the hand
# lets go ON it -- as the original's did -- so a press that wanders off
# before letting go does nothing, which is the one way to change your
# mind about closing a window.  Proved on the About box, whose close
# button about.script already reaches at 295,158.
wait 12
write /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings GlobalMenuBar on
wait 20
click 20 8
wait 4
menu-pick About this system
wait 6
expect-title About this system
note the button up: the gradient runs light at its top-left corner
expect-pixel 293 156 ffea9c
note pressed and held: the window is still here, the button is down
press 295 158
wait 4
expect-title About this system
note and down: the same corner is now the gradient's dark end
expect-pixel 293 156 fbca0a
note the hand wanders off the button and lets go there: nothing happens
move 400 400
wait 4
release 400 400
wait 6
expect-title About this system
note pressed and released ON it: now it closes
click 295 158
wait 6
expect-no-title About this system
quit
